    "title": "The Times Square ball drop is a ship's clock",
    "description": "The Times Square ball copies a tool for telling ships the time: the time ball.\nPorts dropped a ball at the same moment every day so sailors could set their clocks and find their longitude. Greenwich's has dropped at 1 p.m. since 1833. When New York banned the fireworks, the Times' electrician remembered a time ball on the Western Union Building, and the first ball dropped on New Year's Eve 1907.",
